          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b5c3b198d9e470f6cb986361c2444a570b0b72c8",
          "message": "docs: improve contribution guidelines and developer workflow (#612)\n\n* refactor: clean up comments regarding version precedence\n\n- Remove redundant comments about \"last write wins\" and version precedence, as the implementation order is clear from the code.\n- Update the documentation for UseMiseVersions to clarify its role in the overwrite process.\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* docs: update contribution guidelines and add pull request template\n\n- Establish clear \"Lifecycle of a Change\" guide for developers\n- Formalize AI contribution policy and developer expectations\n- Add standard PR template to improve contribution quality and consistency\n- Refine documentation for local setup, testing, and workflow processes\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* docs: update contribution guidelines\n\n- Improve formatting of links and instructions.\n- Add instructions to run snapshot updates before finishing work.\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* feat: add retry-cli and apply to buildkit startup\n\n* Add retry-cli via mise to improve CI reliability.\n* Wrap the buildkit startup command with retry to mitigate transient connection or service availability issues during integration tests.\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* chore: replace retry-cli with local mise task\n\n* Remove external dependency `retry-cli` to reduce toolchain overhead.\n* Add a custom task script to handle command retries with exponential backoff directly within the project.\n* Enable `locked` mode in `mise.toml` to ensure consistent environment versions.\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* chore: disable mise lockfile enforcement\n\n* Commented out `locked` in `mise.toml` to allow for dependency updates without constant lockfile synchronization during development.\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-13T14:31:33-06:00",
