          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d7f531312254d9a532b0a5ec41659b138fe4e354",
          "message": "feat: respect dockerignore on initial source load (#373)\n\n* docs: add claude ref to agents\n\n* refactor: simplify DockerignoreContext passing and make it required\n\n* refactor: another take at fixing the initial docker ignore load stuff\n\n* style: whitespace formatting tweaks\n\nI'm not sure how it got into this state :/\n\n* fix: apply dockerignore rules when copying local app context, not later in the build process\n\n* fix: merge dockerignore excludes with top-level railpack.json excludes/includes\n\n* test: top-level railpack.json exclude/include\n\n* docs: update excluding files docs\n\n* test: add negation to an existing dockerignore to expand test coverage\n\n* fix: hack to determine if I'm understanding the llb exclude functionality right\n\n* refactor: remove Includes and instead use negation operators and Excludes\n\n* test: respect dockerignore on initial source load\n\n- Apply exclude and include filters during the initial buildkit context load to improve local build performance\n- Support top-level exclude and include configurations in railpack.json\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* feat: respect dockerignore on initial source load\n\n- Load local source layers using the plan package directly to ensure .dockerignore patterns are respected at the buildkit level.\n- Prevent unnecessary loading of ignored files like node_modules and virtual environments during local builds.\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* style: formatting updates\n\n* docs(config): update documentation for dockerignore and exclude pattern handling\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* feat(plan): respect dockerignore on initial source load\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* refactor(core): access include rules directly from layer struct\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* feat(buildkit): respect exclude patterns on initial source load\n\n- Apply exclude patterns at the buildkit level during local context loading to prevent transferring unnecessary large directories like node_modules or virtual environments.\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* feat: respect dockerignore on initial source load\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* feat(core): respect dockerignore on initial source load\n\n- Expose the parsed dockerignore context via the build generate context\n- Ensure build results preserve the correct dockerignore metadata and excludes on initial load\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* style(docs): fix trailing whitespace in CLAUDE.md\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* feat(core): respect dockerignore on initial source load\n\n- Apply exclude and include filters during buildkit context setup to avoid loading large ignored directories locally.\n- Support top-level exclude and include configuration in railpack.json.\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* test(plan): assert all expected empty dockerignore examples are found\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* docs(config): fix typo in excluding-files guide\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* feat(dockerignore): respect dockerignore on initial source load\n\n- Apply exclude and include filters during Buildkit context establishment to drastically improve local build performance.\n- Support top-level `exclude` and `include` rules directly in `railpack.json`.\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* docs(config): clarify directory matching behavior in excluding-files guide\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* refactor(core): remove dead dockerignore context fields\n\n- Remove unused dockerignore context properties from build plans and options\n- Clean up obsolete metadata checks in core tests\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit\n\n* feat: add top-level exclude option to railpack config\n\nGenerated-by: aiautocommit",
