          "message": "fix: drop empty env entries instead of keeping explicit empty values (#688)\n\n* fix: drop empty env entries instead of keeping explicit empty values\n\nNAME= entries are now dropped from the environment entirely. Hosted\nbuilders pass every variable as NAME=value including empties, and\nBuildKit cannot mount an empty env secret, so keeping empty variables\nproduced plans referencing secrets the builder never registers\n(failed to solve: secret X not found).\n\nBare NAME entries still inherit from the process environment for local\nCLI use. NAME= must never inherit: variable names are user-controlled\nand would read values out of the build daemon's environment.\n\n* trim comments\n\n* docs: reword empty-value comment to describe behavior only\n\n* single-line comment",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-11T19:34:15Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/railwayapp/railpack/commit/2f38527efef9ca28231abb58289c4737efd8f9fa"
